{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to Abraham.</b> The agent is called by the name of the sender, and therefore Scripture called the angel by the special Name. This is what it means, 'היפלא מה׳' — 'Is anything too wondrous for YHWH' — and it should have said 'from Me,' except that it is the word of the angel; and this is what is meant by 'למועד אשוב' — 'at the appointed time I will return' — for the one who seized Sarah regarding why she laughed is the same one who said, 'at the appointed time I will return to you.'" "<b>Is anything too wondrous for YHWH.</b> The angel Michael says: would it be concealed and the flow of the ה' in your name that is received from YHWH be cut off, so that He would not give you offspring? For just as you stand opposite the attribute of חסד, so shall He give you a son opposite the attribute of דין, for behold, it is incumbent upon Him to complete the chariot above and below: 'למועד אשוב אליך כעת חיה ולשרה בן' — at the appointed time I will return to you, as the time of life, and to Sarah a son."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The phrase היתכסה ויפסק אצילות הה\"א is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. ה\"א read as ה׳ (the divine name). The kabbalistic allusions are rendered as written without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:19.864667814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}